//? Title: OPTICS: actual density ordering and reachability
//? Subtitle: Neighbor/core decisions, linear seed scans and explicit density cuts
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Start with a four-point hand-checkable ordering, then retain the
original132-point mixture of three Gaussian densities and uniform noise.
Canonical neighborhood, reachability-update and seed-selection histories expose
actual implementation work, while undefined distances and the limits of flat
density cuts remain explicit.
)

\toc

> Inclusive neighborhoods and the best available reachability

For generating radius eps, N_eps(p) contains every point at Euclidean
distance≤eps, including p itself. Duplicate coordinate rows remain separate
observations. If at least min_pts neighbors exist, core(p) is the min_pts-th
smallest neighborhood distance; otherwise it is undefined. A processed core
point proposes

$$ reach_{new}(o)=\max(core(p),d(p,o)), \qquad reach(o)\leftarrow\min(reach(o),reach_{new}(o)). $$
\alttext(A core point proposes the larger of its core distance and the target distance; the target retains its smallest discovered reachability.)

The native driver chooses the smallest current seed reachability by a linear
scan. Ties retain the first current seed slot, and removal swaps in the final
seed. This is the actual implementation, rather than a heap-based priority queue
or indexed spatial search. Outer starts visit still-unprocessed original IDs in
ascending order; their reachability remains positive infinity. Each point is
processed once, with all-point neighbor searches and sorted neighborhood
distances.

> A tiny chain and one isolated point

For points[0,.5,1,4], eps=.75,min_pts=2, each point in the first three has core
distance.5. Processing0 discovers1 with reachability.5; processing1 discovers2
at.5. Point3 has only itself, so it is a separate undefined-reachability outer
start and is not a core point. The diagram/table read the actual canonical visit
history.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/optics_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/optics.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::optics_trace({{0.}, {.5}, {1.}, {4.}}, .75, 2);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.visits.size(); ++i) {
        auto &v = t.visits[i];
        d.node(std::to_string(v.point),
               i < 3 ? dm::graphics::DiagramPoint{double(i) * 7, 0}
               : dm::graphics::DiagramPoint{7, -4},
               std::format("Actual point {}\ncore {} reach {}", v.point,
                           v.core_distance, v.reachability));
    }
    d.edge("0", "1").edge("1", "2");
    std::print("| actual order | original point | actual core distance | actual reachability | outer start " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.visits.size(); ++i) {
        auto &v = t.visits[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, v.point, v.core_distance,
                   v.reachability, v.region_start);
    }
    std::print("\nCut labels at.75: `{}`.\n",
               dm::algorithms::optics_extract_dbscan(t.run, .75));
    d.save_svg("build/optics_tiny.svg");
}
```
