| actual order | original point | actual core distance | actual reachability | outer start |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| 0 | 0 | 0.5 | inf | true |
| 1 | 1 | 0.5 | 0.5 | false |
| 2 | 2 | 0.5 | 0.5 | false |
| 3 | 3 | inf | inf | true |

Cut labels at.75: `[0, 0, 0, -1]`.
\image(figures/optics_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual chain visits, isolated outer start and extracted labels for four one-dimensional points.)
\alttext(Positive infinity explicitly marks undefined reachability/core distance rather than an exceptionally large measured distance.)

> Retain the original three-density mixture

The native fixture uses local MT19937_64 seed30: forty points each at(0,0)with
sd.20,(8,0)with sd.70 and(4,7)with sd.35, followed by twelve uniform[-2,10]
coordinate pairs. A fresh normal distribution is constructed for each blob,
preserving the original draw schedule. Standard-library random transforms are
not asserted bitwise portable. These are synthetic method controls, not external
labeled observations.

Run the original eps=5,min_pts=5 and extract at1.2. The plotted profile follows
actual processing order rather than original row ID. Its presentation helper
replaces undefined reachabilities with an explicit finite ceiling only in the
display copy; gray bars mark those replacements. The canonical result retains
infinity. Valleys help inspect density structure, but a cut and a visual valley
do not prove recovery of the generating labels.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/optics_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/optics.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::optics_trace(dm::algorithms::optics_demo_data(), 5., 5);
    auto summary =
        dm::algorithms::optics_cluster_summary(dm::algorithms::optics_extract_dbscan(t.run, 1.2));
    auto profile = dm::algorithms::optics_reachability_profile(t.run.result);
    std::vector<double> undefined_x, undefined_y;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < profile.position.size(); ++i)
        if (profile.undefined[i]) {
            undefined_x.push_back(profile.position[i]);
    undefined_y.push_back(profile.displayed[i]);
        }
        auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
        p.bars(profile.position, profile.displayed, "finite reachability",
               dm::graphics::RGBA{37, 99, 235, 255}, .9);
        if (!undefined_x.empty())
            p.bars(undefined_x, undefined_y, "undefined display",
                   dm::graphics::RGBA{148, 163, 184, 255}, .9);
        p.abline_h(1.2, dm::graphics::RGB{220, 38, 38}, 1.5).title(
            "Original density mixture: actual reachability order").x_label(
            "actual zero-based processing position").y_label(
            "reachability; gray denotes undefined").y_limits(
            0, profile.undefined_height * 1.2).save_svg("build/optics_original.svg");
        std::print("| actual quantity | computed value |\n| --- | --- |\n| original points | {} |\n| processed " "points | {} |\n| extracted cluster sizes at1.2 | `{}` |\n| extracted noise at1.2 | {} |\n| " "actual all-points distance calls | {} |\n| actual linear seed slots scanned | {} |\n| " "undefined reachabilities | {} |\n| presentation-only infinity ceiling | {:.9f} |\n",
                   t.data.size(), t.run.result.ordering.size(), summary.sizes,
                   summary.noise, t.run.work.distance_calls,
                   t.run.work.seed_scan_entries, undefined_x.size(),
                   profile.undefined_height);
}
```
