> Several cuts from one frozen ordering

The extractor scans processing order. If reachability exceeds the cut, a point
starts a new cluster only when its core distance is within the cut; otherwise it
is noise. A point whose reachability is already within the cut inherits the
current cluster. The run-aware overload verifies0≤cut≤the original generating
eps. An old-layout result alone does not retain eps, so its caller is
responsible for that restriction.

This is a conventional reachability-cut labeling, not a guaranteed unique label
vector for every DBSCAN border assignment or proof of the true generating
clusters. Changing min_pts or the generating radius requires another ordering;
changing only an allowed cut reuses this one. The following summaries all use
the same native result, with no refitting, reclustering loop or recomputed
distances in report code.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/optics_cuts.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/optics.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto run =
        dm::algorithms::optics_run(dm::algorithms::optics_demo_data(), 5., 5);
    std::vector<double> cuts{0., .2, .4, .8, 1.2, 2.4, 5.}, noise;
    std::print("| allowed cut | actual cluster sizes | actual noise rows | actual labeled rows |\n| ---: | " "--- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (double cut : cuts) {
        auto s =
            dm::algorithms::optics_cluster_summary(dm::algorithms::optics_extract_dbscan(run, cut));
        noise.push_back(s.noise);
        std::print("| {} | `{}` | {} | {} |\n", cut, s.sizes, s.noise,
                   s.labels.size() - s.noise);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.lines(cuts, noise, "actual noise count",
            dm::graphics::RGBA{37, 99, 235, 255}).points(
        cuts, noise, dm::graphics::RGBA{37, 99, 235, 255}, 3.);
    p.title("One frozen OPTICS ordering: actual cut summaries").x_label(
        "allowed extraction cut").y_label("actual noise-labeled rows").save_svg(
        "build/optics_cuts.svg");
}
```
