> Work, undefined values and complete contracts

Successful runs query each point once against every point, giving N² distance
calls. Sorting neighborhood distances and linear scans of seed candidates lead
to O(N²(D+log N)) worst-case work for D-dimensional points; this implementation
makes no heap or spatial-index performance claim. Ordinary state is linear in N
beyond the input, with no all-pairs distance matrix. Safe original double
distance order is retained; nonfinite differences/squared sums select a checked
complete long-double hypot route. A distance not representable as finite double
throws rather than being confused with the intentional undefined-distance
sentinel.

Complete finite rectangular coordinates, finite nonnegative radius and positive
min_pts are validated before allocation/search. Self counts as a neighbor, exact
radius ties are included, duplicate points are separate observations, and a
zero-dimensional row is accepted as a point at zero distance from every matching
row. min_pts>N makes every point noncore; an empty dataset remains empty.

Owned trace admission counts controls2, input coordinatesND, result entries3N,
each neighborhood record1+2K neighbor entries, each update1, each extraction1+2K
seed/priority entries and each visit1. Default1000000 logical units, zero
disables. Detailed history can be quadratic; record fields, capacities and
allocator overhead are excluded from that policy. Admission precedes retained
copies/appends, no partial trace is returned on failure, and no caller
references or global mutable state remain.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/optics_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/optics.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<std::vector<std::vector<double>> > data{{}, {{0.}, {0.}},
                                                        {{0.}, {2.}, {4.}},
                                                        {{}, {}, {}},
                                                        {{0.}, {1.}},
                                                        {{0.}, {1e200}}};
    std::vector<double> eps{0., 0., .1, 0., 2., 1e201};
    std::vector<std::size_t> minimum{1, 2, 2, 2, 5, 2};
    std::vector<std::string> labels{"empty", "duplicates", "isolated",
                                    "zero dimension", "too few neighbors",
                                    "wide distance"};
    std::vector<double> distances;
    std::print("| explicit control | actual distance calls | actual seed extractions | actual widened " "distances | actual processing order |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < data.size(); ++i) {
        auto r = dm::algorithms::optics_run(data[i], eps[i], minimum[i]);
        distances.push_back(r.work.distance_calls);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | `{}` |\n", labels[i],
                   r.work.distance_calls, r.work.seed_extractions,
                   r.work.widened_distances, r.result.ordering);
    }
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(distances, labels, "actual distance calls");
    p.title("OPTICS controls: actual all-points search work").x_label(
        "explicit input/control").y_label("actual original-distance attempts").save_svg("build/optics_controls.svg");
}
```
